entries.description:
When a die is rolled once, there are six equally likely outcomes
ξ = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}
Let A be the event ‘a number greater than four is obtained’.
Then A = {5, 6}
Hence, P(A) = 2/6 = 1/3

The events A and B are:
A = {3, 6, 9, 12}
B = {6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12}
and A ∩ B = {6, 9, 12}
Here is the Venn diagram illustrating these events.
